  "title": "More ways to generate text",
  "summary": "January broadened the text and image APIs while rebuilding the homepage around the tools and community projects people make with them.\n\nDeepSeek-V3 and reasoning models, GPT-4o, and Scaleway-backed options expanded the text API. JSON mode, vision examples, model routing, and requested temperature received practical fixes.\n\nThe API added structured errors and steadier per-IP queueing, repaired generation tracking, and raised its request limit to 200 per minute. Feed events also stopped including requester IP addresses.\n\nImages now default to 1024×1024, requested dimensions map to supported aspect ratios, and explicit prompt-enhancement settings are respected. Prompt handling was corrected to preserve non-Latin text, while valid priority tokens gained a path around the per-IP queue.\n\nThe homepage rebuild refreshed the image tools, examples, and project directory. Restored listings, a GitHub issue form for project submissions, and links to new community apps made the surrounding ecosystem easier to explore.",
